WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.763
Jamming or strong interference can reduce signal quality or prevent a receiver from maintaining satellite lock.

00:00:06.763 --> 00:00:11.343
Possible effects include fewer usable satellites, poor accuracy estimates, navigation warnings,

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:15.091
delayed position updates, or loss of position-dependent flight modes.

00:00:15.091 --> 00:00:21.754
The aircraft may drift or hold position less reliably when it transitions away from satellite-assisted stabilization.

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:26.334
Automated missions can pause, abort, or behave according to a failsafe.

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:30.082
The exact response depends on the aircraft and configuration.

00:00:30.082 --> 00:00:34.246
Unexpected return behavior or a navigation-mode change deserves immediate attention.

00:00:34.246 --> 00:00:37.994
Read warnings, maintain visual awareness, and reduce mission complexity.

00:00:37.994 --> 00:00:42.575
Do not dismiss an alert because the map still looks plausible.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:45.073
Similar symptoms can have non-malicious causes.

00:00:45.073 --> 00:00:47.988
Buildings, terrain, foliage, antenna orientation, reflected signals,

00:00:47.988 --> 00:00:50.487
weather-related obstruction, power infrastructure, damaged equipment,

00:00:50.487 --> 00:00:52.985
or software faults can degrade reception.

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:58.399
Localized radio noise from faulty or incompatible equipment can also resemble intentional interference.

00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:02.979
Note whether the problem follows one aircraft, one controller, one location,

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:05.894
or multiple independent systems before drawing conclusions.

00:01:05.894 --> 00:01:11.308
Look for a pattern across multiple indicators: satellite count or status, quality estimates,

00:01:11.308 --> 00:01:14.639
map behavior, visual position, flight-mode changes, compass information,

00:01:14.639 --> 00:01:16.305
and the physical environment.

00:01:16.305 --> 00:01:19.220
A single changing number remains weak evidence.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.302
The safety response is conservative.

00:01:21.302 --> 00:01:25.882
Stop automated collection, keep the aircraft in sight, avoid flying farther,

00:01:25.882 --> 00:01:30.047
and return or land using trained procedures before battery, signal,

00:01:30.047 --> 00:01:31.712
or orientation margins narrow.

00:01:31.712 --> 00:01:35.460
Diagnose cause after the aircraft and people are safe.
